 ## Background
-Solid Voxelization via Octree is a technique to convert a set of 3D line segments into a solid voxel representation using an octree data structure [S1, unofficial]. It is used in real-time rendering applications, as demonstrated by the accompanying GPU-based ray tracer in the source code [S1, unofficial].
+Solid Voxelization via Octree is a technique to convert a set of 3D line segments into a solid voxel representation using an octree data structure [S1, unofficial]. It was developed by Mike-Leo-Smith for the SolidVoxelization project [S1, unofficial]. It is used in real-time rendering applications, as demonstrated by the accompanying GPU-based ray tracer in the source code [S1, unofficial].
 
